  <div class="modules-wrapper">
    <div class="hero-modules">
      <h1><i class="fas fa-cubes"></i> FSCSS Modules & Libraries</h1>
      <p>A guide to understanding the FSCSS package ecosystem — how libraries are structured, registered, and imported.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- What Is This? -->
    <div class="section-card">
      <div class="section-title"><i class="fas fa-question-circle"></i> What Is This?</div>
      <p>The <a href="https://github.com/fscss-ttr/fscss-modules" target="_blank" style="color:#60a5fa;">fscss-modules</a> registry is the central discovery hub for FSCSS-compatible libraries. It powers the <strong><a href="https://fscss.devtem.org/libraries" style="color:#60a5fa;">FSCSS Libraries page</a></strong> — where developers can browse, learn about, and import available community and core plugins.</p>
      <div class="info-note"><i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> Submitting here <strong>does not</strong> automatically make your library importable by name. That's a separate step covered below.</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Understanding package.json -->
    <div class="section-card">
      <div class="section-title"><i class="fas fa-file-code"></i> Understanding <code class="code-inline">package.json</code></div>
      <p>Every FSCSS library should include a <code class="code-inline">package.json</code> at its root. Here's a full example with each field explained:</p>
      <div class="json-block">
        <span class="punc-json">{</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"name"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="str-json">"st-core"</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"version"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="str-json">"1.1.0"</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"description"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="str-json">"Lightweight FSCSS-based UI library for statistical dashboards and components"</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"extension"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="str-json">"fscss"</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"fscss_version"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="str-json">"^1.1.24"</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"blocked_methods"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="punc-json">[]</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"repository"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="punc-json">{</span> <span class="str-json">"type"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="str-json">"git"</span><span class="punc-json">,</span> <span class="str-json">"url"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="str-json">"https://github.com/fscss-ttr/st-core.fscss"</span> <span class="punc-json">}</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"file"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="punc-json">{</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"usage"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="punc-json">{</span> <span class="str-json">"directive"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="str-json">"st-*"</span><span class="punc-json">,</span> <span class="str-json">"helpers"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="punc-json">[</span><span class="str-json">"st-root"</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><span class="str-json">"st-container"</span><span class="punc-json">]</span> <span class="punc-json">}</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"modules"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="punc-json">[</span><span class="str-json">"./st-core.fscss"</span><span class="punc-json">]</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"remote"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="str-json">"./st-core.fscss"</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="punc-json">}</span><br>
        <span class="punc-json">}</span>
      </div>
      <table class="field-table">
        <tr><th><code>name</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e; font-size:0.8rem;"></i> Short identifier (no .fscss suffix needed)</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>version</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> Semantic version — bump on every release</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>description</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> One-line summary shown on libraries page</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>extension</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> Must be <code>"fscss"</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>fscss_version</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> Minimum compiler version (semver range)</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>blocked_methods</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> Array of disabled built‑ins. Leave <code>[]</code> if none</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>repository</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> GitHub repo URL</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>bugs</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-thumbs-up" style="color:#f59e0b;"></i> recommended – issues URL</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>file.usage.directive</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> Mixin prefix pattern (e.g. <code>st-*</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>file.usage.helpers</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> Explicit list of all public mixins/helpers</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>file.modules</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> Array of relative paths to all .fscss source files</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>file.remote</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> Single entry-point file for remote <code>@import</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>author</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-thumbs-up" style="color:#f59e0b;"></i> recommended – shown on discovery card</td></tr>
        <tr><th><code>license</code></th><td><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color:#22c55e;"></i> MIT strongly recommended</td></tr>
       </table>
    </div>

    <!-- The Two Steps: Discover vs Import by Name -->
    <div class="section-card">
      <div class="section-title"><i class="fas fa-code-branch"></i> Discover vs. Import by Name</div>
      <p>There's an important distinction between <strong>listing</strong> your library and making it <strong>named-importable</strong>.</p>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin:0.5rem 0 0.2rem;"><i class="fas fa-eye"></i> Step 1 — List in the Registry (Discovery Only)</h3>
        <p>Submit a PR to <code class="code-inline">fscss-ttr/FSCSS/edit/main/assets/scripts/libs.json</code> adding your repo URL:</p>
        <div class="json-block">
          <span class="punc-json">{</span><br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"remotes"</span><span class="punc-json">:</span> <span class="punc-json">[</span><br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"https://github.com/fscss-ttr/st-core.fscss"</span><span class="punc-json">,</span><br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="str-json">"https://github.com/Figsh/counterx.fscss"</span><br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="punc-json">]</span><br>
          <span class="punc-json">}</span>
        </div>
        <p>This makes your library <strong>visible</strong> at <a href="https://fscss.devtem.org/libraries" style="color:#60a5fa;">fscss.devtem.org/libraries</a>. Users can find and read about your lib here.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin:0.5rem 0 0.2rem;"><i class="fas fa-sign-in-alt"></i> Step 2 — Named Import Support (Full Integration)</h3>
        <p>To allow <code class="code-inline">@import((*) from your-lib)</code>, your entry file must be added to the FSCSS core folder: <code class="code-inline">/xf/styles/</code>. Until then, users import via full URL:</p>
        <div class="json-block" style="background:#0a0f1c;">
          @import((*) from "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/.../main/lib.fscss")
        </div>
        <div class="info-note"><i class="fas fa-clipboard-list"></i> See the <a href="https://fscss.devtem.org/submit-guide" style="color:#60a5fa;">Submit Guide</a> for the full walkthrough.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Entry File Requirements -->
    <div class="section-card">
      <div class="section-title"><i class="fas fa-file-alt"></i> Entry File Requirements</div>
      <p>Your library must expose a <strong>single entry file</strong> — either <code class="code-inline">index.fscss</code> or <code class="code-inline">your-lib-name.fscss</code>. This file should either contain all source directly or import internal modules, acting as a complete single-file bundle. The <code class="code-inline">file.remote</code> field in <code>package.json</code> must point to this file.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Ecosystem Libraries -->
    <div class="section-card">
      <div class="section-title"><i class="fas fa-leaf"></i> Ecosystem Libraries</div>
      <div class="library-grid">
        <div class="lib-card"><h3><i class="fas fa-chart-line"></i> st-core.fscss</h3><p>Pure CSS statistical charts & dashboards – line charts, dot plots, clip‑path driven. Zero JS.</p><a class="lib-link" href="https://github.com/fscss-ttr/st-core.fscss" target="_blank">github.com/fscss-ttr/st-core.fscss <i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i></a></div>
